    {
      "contentTypeKey": "3ef5c851-77d2-46af-9a22-e2bfadd01829",
      "udi": "umb://element/f63f1abbf92b407d96eecb7060142f8a",
      "title": "On-Site Investigations",
      "content": {
        "markup": "<p>On-site asphalt testing provides immediate feedback on material quality and construction processes during roadworks.</p>\n<p>Tests such as extracting and testing core samples from compacted asphalt layers allow engineers to assess whether asphalt mixtures are compacted correctly and meet layer thickness requirements.</p>\n<p>Additional tests like, Marvill permeability, IRI, MMLS &amp; Rolling straight edge help confirm that the asphalt conforms to design and construction specifications, ensuring early detection of potential issues like under-<br>compaction, incorrect binder content, rutting &amp; rideability.</p>\n<p>By conducting these tests on-site, project&nbsp;teams can make timely adjustments and prevent costly failures or rework.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>On-site testing is essential for maintaining control over quality during all phases of construction.</p>",
        "blocks": {
          "contentData": [],
          "settingsData": []
        }
      },
      "images": [
        {
          "key": "ad30a7b6-0d5e-414c-80c5-7a8b452937f2",
          "mediaKey": "08c1492b-6183-4146-af7a-5153a18f57a1"
        }
      ],
      "anchorID": ""
    },
